practice.task:
The reference bug. Predict the output, run it, explain it in one sentence:

$a = [1, 2, 3];
foreach ($a as &$v) { $v *= 2; }
foreach ($a as $v) { }
print_r($a);

practice.solution:
```php
Array ( [0] => 2 [1] => 4 [2] => 4 )

// After loop 1, $v still references $a[2]. Loop 2 assigns each element INTO that reference,
// so $a[2] becomes 2, then 4, then 4 (itself). Fix: unset($v) after a by-reference loop,
// or avoid &: $a = array_map(fn($x) => $x * 2, $a);
```
